/* book Worked example: Q: A UPI fraud classifier has N = 1000 labelled transactions. You train with mini-batch gradient descent using B = 100 for 20 epochs. (a) How many iterations per epoch? (b) How many weight updates? (c) How many updates would full-batch gradient descent make in the same 20 epochs? (d) One sample's gradient has variance 0.4. Find the variance and standard deviation of the mini-batch gradient, assuming independent samples.
   1. Iterations per epoch = N/B = 1000/100 = 10 iterations per epoch.
   2. Weight updates in 20 epochs = epochs × iterations per epoch = 20 × 10 = 200 updates.
   3. Full-batch gradient descent makes one update per epoch, so 20 epochs × 1 = 20 updates.
   4. Mini-batch variance = σ²/B = 0.4/100 = 0.004.
   5. Mini-batch standard deviation = √0.004 ≈ 0.0632, rounded to 0.063 gradient units.
   Answer: With B = 100 there are 10 iterations per epoch, 200 weight updates in 20 epochs, 20 full-batch updates, and the mini-batch gradient has variance 0.004 and standard deviation about 0.063 gradient units. */
